WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.520
A whale swims in the sea.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.300
Its body is shaped like a fish.

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.920
Yet a whale breathes air with lungs, and it feeds its young milk.

4
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.180
Its closest living relatives are hippos.

5
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.500
So how do scientists figure out who is related to whom?

6
00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:26.453
Scientists group living things by how they are related.

7
00:00:27.113 --> 00:00:28.453
This is called classification.

8
00:00:29.553 --> 00:00:32.593
They do not group by looks, home, or diet.

9
00:00:33.213 --> 00:00:36.253
Those can match in animals that are not close relatives.

10
00:00:37.193 --> 00:00:43.693
Instead, they compare inherited evidence: body parts, embryos, fossils, and DNA.

11
00:00:44.673 --> 00:00:47.973
They trust a grouping most when the kinds of evidence agree.

12
00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:52.703
Look at the front limb of a human, a bat, and a whale.

13
00:00:53.563 --> 00:00:57.683
A hand grasps, a wing flies, a flipper steers.

14
00:00:58.483 --> 00:01:04.583
Yet each has one upper arm bone, two forearm bones, wrist bones, and finger bones.

15
00:01:05.743 --> 00:01:08.883
Parts built the same way are called homologous structures.

16
00:01:09.563 --> 00:01:11.523
They were inherited from a common ancestor.

17
00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:16.147
Embryos can share parts that adults lose.

18
00:01:17.247 --> 00:01:21.267
Early fish, chick, and human embryos all have a tail.

19
00:01:22.087 --> 00:01:26.427
They also have a row of folds in the neck, called pharyngeal arches.

20
00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:30.527
In fish, several arches go on to support gills.

21
00:01:31.307 --> 00:01:35.147
In humans, they become parts of the jaw, ear, and throat.

22
00:01:36.227 --> 00:01:38.987
Human embryos do not turn into fish first.

23
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.840
A cladogram is a branching diagram.

24
00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:47.400
It shows the order in which groups split from common ancestors.

25
00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.300
It is built from shared derived characteristics.

26
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.220
That is a trait that first appeared in one ancestor and passed to its descendants.

27
00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.560
Hair is one. Mammals share it, and fish and frogs do not.

28
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.010
Now place the whale.

29
00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:09.490
Lungs and milk put it with the mammals, not the fish.

30
00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:16.970
Fossil whales with legs, embryos, and DNA it shares with hippos all point the same

31
00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.730
way. The fishlike shape fits life in water.

32
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:26.810
Keep this rule: judge relatives by inherited traits, not by looks.
